WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.345
Decision tools help teams make reasoning visible.

2
00:00:03.345 --> 00:00:06.924
A decision matrix compares options against criteria.

3
00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:10.269
Weighted criteria show which factors matter more.

4
00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:16.260
A decision tree maps choices, uncertain events, and possible consequences at a high level.

5
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:22.017
A risk register captures risks, likelihood, impact, owners, mitigations, and status.

6
00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:26.840
These tools are useful when they support judgment rather than replace it.

7
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:33.842
Cost-benefit thinking helps teams compare what an option requires against what it is expected to produce.

8
00:00:33.842 --> 00:00:35.554
The cost is not only money.

9
00:00:35.554 --> 00:00:43.333
It can include time, attention, operational burden, technical debt, training, disruption, and loss of optionality.

10
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:49.946
Benefits can include safety, reliability, revenue, learning, trust, resilience, or reduced risk.

11
00:00:49.946 --> 00:00:52.591
Good analysis makes both sides visible.

12
00:00:52.591 --> 00:00:58.348
Decision records are especially valuable in technical and operational environments.

13
00:00:58.348 --> 00:01:08.851
A good record captures the frame, decision owner, options considered, criteria, evidence, assumptions, tradeoffs, risks, and the reason for the chosen path.

14
00:01:08.851 --> 00:01:12.897
It also records what would cause the decision to be revisited.

15
00:01:12.897 --> 00:01:16.631
This makes decisions reviewable instead of mysterious.

16
00:01:16.631 --> 00:01:18.887
Team decisions need role clarity.

17
00:01:18.887 --> 00:01:26.433
People should know who is giving input, who is advising, who is deciding, who is executing, and who must be informed.

18
00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:32.891
Disagreement should be welcomed when it improves the decision, but it also needs a path to closure.

19
00:01:32.891 --> 00:01:43.860
Psychological safety, in practical terms, means people can raise concerns, share uncertainty, and challenge assumptions without being punished for useful candor.

20
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.350
After-action reviews close the loop.

21
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:55.608
They compare expected results with actual outcomes, examine what was known at the time, and identify what should change in future decisions.

22
00:01:55.608 --> 00:01:59.031
The best teams do not use tools to perform certainty.

23
00:01:59.031 --> 00:02:04.321
They use tools to clarify judgment, create accountability, and learn over time.
